<title>GERMANY: Lufthansa details Q1 traffic figures.</title>
<headline>Lufthansa details Q1 traffic figures.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three months to March 31, 1997</p>
<p>Lufthansa Group:</p>
<p>    Passengers (in thousands)		9,186   up 1.3 pct</p>
<p>    Cargo/mail (in thousands tonnes)     397.8   down 0.4 pct</p>
<p>    Available seat-km (millions)	   28,099  up 5.6 pct</p>
<p>    Revenue passenger-km (millions)	19,726  up 10.8 pct</p>
<p>    Passenger load factor (percent)	70.2    up 3.3 pct pts</p>
<p>    Available tonne-km (millions)	  4,985   up 4.8 pct</p>
<p>    Revenue tonne-km (millions)	    3,477   up 6.7 pct</p>
<p>    Overall load factor (percent)	  69.7    up 1.2 pct pts</p>
<p>    Number of flights			  147,144 up 4.2 pct</p>
<p>Lufthansa also gave the following breakdown for its operating units:</p>
<p>Deutsche Lufthansa AG (scheduled passenger service)</p>
<p>    Passengers (in thousands)		7,209   down 1.2 pct</p>
<p>    Available seat-km (millions)	   21,820  up 4.9 pct</p>
<p>    Revenue passenger-km (millions)	14,932  up 11.6 pct</p>
<p>    Passenger load factor (percent)	68.4    up 4.1 pct pts</p>
<p>    Number of flights			  79,915  down 2.7 pct</p>
<p>Condor Flugdienst GmbH (charter airline service)</p>
<p>    Passengers (in thousands)		1,211   up 8.6 pct</p>
<p>    Available seat-km (millions)	   5,351   up 6.2 pct</p>
<p>    Revenue passenger-km (millions)	4,350   up 7.2 pct</p>
<p>    Passenger load factor (percent)	81.3    up 0.8 pct</p>
<p>    Number of flights			  6,613   up 11.7 pct</p>
<p>Lufthansa Cargo AG (cargo airline service)</p>
<p>    Cargo/mail (thousands tonnes)	  397.8   down 0.4 pct</p>
<p>    Available cargo tonne-km (millions)  2,230   up 3.5 pct</p>
<p>    Revenue cargo tonne-km (millions)    1,522   up 1.7 pct</p>
<p>    Cargo load factor (percent)	    68.3    dn 1.2 pct pts</p>
<p>    Number of flights			  33,747  up 13.9 pct</p>
<p>Lufthansa CityLine GmbH (regional airline service)</p>
<p>    Passengers (in thousands)		765     up 16.1 pct</p>
<p>    Available seat-km (millions)	   928     up 20.4 pct</p>
<p>    Revenue passenger-km (millions)	444     up 18.3 pct</p>
<p>    Passenger load factor (percent)	47.8    dn 0.9 pct pts</p>
<p>    Number of flights			  26,869  up 14.5 pct</p>
<p>Lufthansa also gave the following breakdown on its regional operations.</p>
<p>European operations, including Germany:</p>
<p>    Passengers (in thousands)		7,171   down 2.0 pct</p>
<p>    Cargo/mail (in thousands tonnes)     179.3   down 4.1 pct</p>
<p>    Available tonne-km (millions)	  1,261   up 2.2 pct</p>
<p>    Revenue tonne-km (millions)	    692     up 0.9 pct</p>
<p>    Overall load factor (percent)	  54.8    dn 0.7 pct pts</p>
<p>North and South America operations:</p>
<p>    Passengers (in thousands)		991     up 18.5 pct</p>
<p>    Cargo/mail (in thousands tonnes)     106.9   up 3.9 pct</p>
<p>    Available tonne-km (millions)	  1,827   up 6.5 pct</p>
<p>    Revenue tonne-km (millions)	    1,397   up 10.8 pct</p>
<p>    Overall load factor (percent)	  76.5    up 3.0 pct pts</p>
<p>Asia-Pacific, Middle East and Africa operations:</p>
<p>    Passengers (in thousands)		1,010   up 11.8 pct</p>
<p>    Cargo/mail (in thousands)		98.7    up 2.9 pct</p>
<p>    Available tonne-km (millions)	  1,864   up 4.1 pct</p>
<p>    Revenue tonne-km (millions)	    1,367   up 4.9 pct</p>
<p>    Overall load factor (percent)	  73.4    up 0.6 pct pts</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of the German airline is Deutsche Lufthansa AG.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
